<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="48190" href="schedule/2019/spring/PSYC/593/48190.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120191" href="schedule/2019/spring.xml">Spring 2019</term><subject id="PSYC" href="schedule/2019/spring/PSYC.xml">Psychology</subject><course id="593" href="schedule/2019/spring/PSYC/593.xml">Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>MF </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Psyc &amp; Neuroscience of Aging</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This class offers a broad survey of the psychology and neuroscience of aging.  The three units will cover (1) demographics, neuroscience, and health; (2) Cognitive neuroscience of aging; and (3) Age-related pathologies and psychopathology.  In addition to class attendance and 3 midterm exams (one per unit) graduate students will be required to write a comprehensive review paper on a topic of their choice relevant to the class.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2019-05-01Z</endDate><specialApproval>Instructor Approval Required</specialApproval><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="CNF">Conference</type><start>ARRANGED</start><instructors><instructor lastName="Fabiani" firstName="M">Fabiani, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>